/-!
# GAP-A (`EscapeShort`) for `n = 3`: `Work.Mostow.gapA_three`

`gapA_three` says: for a lattice `Γ ≤ PO 3 1` with the multiplicity-thick hypothesis
(`MultThickProp`, used only through `frameThinFar`), and for every `ε > 0`, outside a compact set
some `γ ∈ Γ` of infinite order moves `u` by less than `ε`.

## Route

The proof is the assembly of the design pieces of `REFS/lead-design/NOTES_LEAD_gapA.md`:

* `Work.Mostow.frameThinFar` (proved): outside a compact set some `γ ≠ 1` is `η`-near-identity
  at `u`. If `γ` has infinite order it is already `η ≤ ε`-short, and we are done;
* otherwise `γ` is torsion, and the **torsion branch** below produces an infinite-order
  `η`-short element for `η` below a threshold depending only on `Γ` and `ε`.

The torsion branch (`torsionBranch_of_pieces`) combines:

* `gapA.rotData3` — S3+S4+S5: a finite-order `f` which is near-identity at `z` is a rotation
  `IsRotationAbout f a b θ` about a geodesic; the pointwise stabiliser of that geodesic is
  generated by a rotation `b₀` of order `M`, `f = b₀^k`;
* `gapA.depthPlus3` — the "+1" depth bound `sinh (distGeod a b z + 1) sin (π/M) ≤ (π/2) sinh (η/2)`
  (hence `M ≥ 3`), obtained from `NearIdAt` applied at a point one unit further away from the axis
  (`gapA.distGeod_addOne`);
* `gapA.conjCount3` — S6 (ConjCount): conjugates of `b₀` that are near-identity at a common point
  are `b₀^{±1}`;
* `gapA.unfoldTube` — S7: `volH 3 (Tb b₀ η₁ ∩ Dc) ≤ 2 * volH 3 D`;
* `gapA.tubeIneq3` — S9: the dichotomy "a translation of the axis exists, with the tube-volume
  lower bound `ℓ (π/M) sinh²ρ/2`, or every fundamental domain meets `Tb b₀ η₁` in infinite
  volume"; the second case contradicts `unfoldTube` and `exists_fundamentalDomain` (proved);
* `gapA.screwShort3` — S10: the screw `g * b₀^j` has infinite order and moves every point by at
  most `2 (ℓ + π/M) cosh (distGeod a b z)`;
* `gapA.screwNumeric` — the real-arithmetic core turning the tube-volume bound, the depth bound
  and the screw bound into `hdist z (g' z) ≤ 300 (V/η_Z² + 1) η`.

With `V = volH 3 D` (the covolume of `Γ`) and `η_c := min (min (1/8) (η_Z/20))
(ε / (2 * (1200 * (V/η_Z² + 1))))` the screw `g'` is `ε`-short at `z`.
-/

namespace Work.Mostow

open Submission.Mostow LeanEval.Geometry.MostowRigidity MeasureTheory
open Work.Mostow.gapA
open scoped ENNReal



open Submission.Mostow LeanEval.Geometry.MostowRigidity MeasureTheory
